    {
      "id": "8-the-one-thing-to-remember",
      "title": "8. The One Thing to Remember",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If you remember nothing else, remember this:",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "<strong>Count how many times the most-repeated operation runs as a function of&nbsp;<code>n</code>, keep the dominant term, and drop everything else.</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every time complexity analysis you ever do is just answering that one question.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Start applying this to every piece of code you write or read. After a few weeks, it becomes instinct you'll&nbsp;<em>see</em>&nbsp;the&nbsp;<code>O(n²)</code>in a nested loop before you even finish reading it.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
